<title>USA: Hashimoto calls forex markets &quot;calm&quot;.</title>
<headline>Hashimoto calls forex markets &quot;calm&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto said on Thursday that foreign exchange markets were very calm.</p>
<p>&quot;If you look at the situation in the foreign exchange market, the market has been calm, very calm,&quot; Hashimoto said in an unprompted opening statement to reporters before his meeting with U.S. President Bill Clinton.</p>
<p>The two leaders are here for a summit of the Group of Seven industrialized nations and Russia.  </p>
<p>Hashimoto made his remark about the stability of the foreign exchange markets immediately after Clinton had said he wished the U.S.-Japan trade deficit were not so high and that he intended to discuss the matter with the Japanese Prime Minister.</p>
</text>
